Title: The Third Eye (test scene)
Credit: written by
Author: Colby Gutierrez-Kraybill
Draft date: 2026-10-18
Notes: Pipeline test — key frames, in-betweens, sound, Scratch. ~55 s. May never be used.

/* CODUBEE: flat black cat, white eyes. Two eyes until the end of this scene.
   FRIEND is a placeholder: a second cat, not yet designed. It could equally be a
   sibling (see the note at the end); nothing in the action depends on which. */

EXT. BACK GARDEN - MORNING

Sunlight. Tall grass. A moth bobs past.

A tiny black kitten, CODUBEE (two eyes), pounces — misses — tumbles — springs up delighted and bats at a dandelion until it bursts into seeds.

CODUBEE
(giggling)
Again!

Seeds drift up and become...

EXT. ALLEY BEHIND THE GARDEN - DUSK

...falling leaves. Years later. CODUBEE, now a lanky teen, trots along the top of a fence beside FRIEND, a cat the same age. They bump shoulders. Easy. Close.

FRIEND
Race you to the yard.

A low GROWL from the dark below. A DOG'S SHADOW slides across the fence boards. BARKING.

They bolt along the alley. The dog's shadow grows behind them.

Ahead: a gap under a fence. Only room for one.

Codubee reaches it first — turns to let Friend through —

Friend SHOVES Codubee aside, slips under the fence alone.

Codubee skids. Fence boards RATTLE. Snarling right behind.

Codubee scrambles up the fence and over — barely.

EXT. YARD - CONTINUOUS

Codubee drops onto the far side. Panting. Safe.

Friend sits a few feet away, licking a paw. Unhurried. Glances at Codubee. A small, satisfied look.

Then turns and walks off without a word.

Codubee watches them go. Silence except breathing.

CLOSE ON CODUBEE

Their two eyes fill with understanding.

On their forehead, a seam of light. A THIRD EYE opens for the first time.

It sees clearly. And it is the only eye that cries.

A single tear runs from the third eye.

Rain begins.

FADE OUT.

/* NOTE (sibling variant): replace FRIEND with a sibling; add one line early in the
   garden scene showing them as kittens together, so the shove reads as family. */
